below are some samples of how to use `github.com/nalgeon/be`

```bash
✅ require.NoError(t, err) → be.Err(t, err, nil)
✅ assert.Equal(t, expected, actual) → be.Equal(t, actual, expected) (parameter order reversed!)
✅ assert.Error(t, err) → be.True(t, err != nil)
✅ assert.True/False(t, x) → be.True(t, x) / be.True(t, !x)
✅ require.IsType(t, qm.OrderBy(""), x) → Type assertions with be.True(t, ok)
```

## test best practices

```
# - t.Parallel() can be used in each test suite or subtest
# - use table driven test structure
# - error handling logic
# - expected behavior of test cases
# - if you need you can write a common concerns setup and teardown function into the MainTest and TestSuite level
```

## When to use Parallel

```go
func TestPureFunction(t *testing.T) {
    t.Parallel() // ✅ main test can be parallel

    for _, tt := range tests {
        t.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {
            t.Parallel() // ✅ child test can also be parallel

            // test logic...
        })
    }
}
```

## When not to use Parallel

**do not use `t.Parallel()` to avoid race condition**

```go
var globalVar = "initial"

func TestFunctionModifyingGlobal(t *testing.T) {
    // ❌ do not use t.Parallel() - modifying global variable will cause race condition

    for _, tt := range tests {
        t.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {
            // ❌ child test also do not use t.Parallel()
            // do not use t.Parallel() because modifying global variable will cause race condition

            // save original value
            original := globalVar
            defer func() {
                globalVar = original // restore original value
            }()

            // modify global variable for test
            globalVar = tt.testValue

            // test logic...
        })
    }
}
```

## use table driven test structure

### business layer or db layer

test case that need a MockDependency which usually at business layer or db layer

```go
tcs := map[string]struct {
    name           string
    input          InputType
    mockSetup      func(*MockDependency)
    expectedOutput OutputType
    expectedError  string
}{
    "success_case": {
        input: InputType{Field1: "value1", Field2: 123},
        mockSetup: func(mock *MockDependency) {
            mock.On("Method", mock.Anything).Return(expectedResult, nil)
        },
        expectedOutput: OutputType{Field: "expected"},
    },
    "error_case": {
        input: InputType{Field1: ""},
        expectedError: "input cannot be empty",
    },
}

for name, tc := range tcs {
    t.Run(name, func(t *testing.T) {
        t.Parallel()

        // Given: 准备 mock
        mockDep := NewMockDependency(t)
        if tc.mockSetup != nil {
            tc.mockSetup(mockDep)
        }

        // When: 执行测试
        service := NewService(mockDep)
        result, err := service.Method(tc.input)

        // Then: 验证结果
        if tc.expectedError != "" {
            be.True(t, err != nil)
            be.True(t, strings.Contains(err.Error(), tc.expectedError))
            return
        }

        be.Err(t, err, nil)
        be.Equal(t, result, tc.expectedOutput)
        mockDep.AssertExpectations(t)
    })
}
```

## test cases for api layer

API layer tests use stub functions instead of mocks, and test HTTP handlers with request/response validation.

```go
func TestAPI_handlerName(t *testing.T) {
    t.Parallel()

    const iamID = "iam-123"
    wantOutput := SomeOutput{
        Field1: "value1",
        Field2: 123,
    }

    testCases := []struct {
        name           string
        method         string
        path           string
        reqBody        string
        prepareRequest func(*http.Request) *http.Request
        stubFactory    func(*testing.T) *apiStubs
        wantStatusCode int
        wantRespBody   string
    }{
        {
            name:   "success",
            method: http.MethodGet,
            path:   "/gateway/authenticated/v1/endpoint",
            prepareRequest: func(req *http.Request) *http.Request {
                return withUserProfile(req, iamID)
            },
            stubFactory: func(t *testing.T) *apiStubs {
                return &apiStubs{
                    app: &stubApp{
                        methodFunc: func(ctx context.Context, gotIAM string) (SomeOutput, error) {
                            be.Equal(t, gotIAM, iamID)
                            return wantOutput, nil
                        },
                    },
                }
            },
            wantStatusCode: http.StatusOK,
            wantRespBody:   `{"field1":"value1","field2":123}`,
        },
        {
            name:           "unauthenticated",
            method:         http.MethodGet,
            path:           "/gateway/authenticated/v1/endpoint",
            wantStatusCode: http.StatusUnauthorized,
            wantRespBody:   `{"error":"unauthenticated","error_description":"unauthenticated"}`,
        },
        {
            name:   "app_error",
            method: http.MethodGet,
            path:   "/gateway/authenticated/v1/endpoint",
            prepareRequest: func(req *http.Request) *http.Request {
                return withUserProfile(req, iamID)
            },
            stubFactory: func(t *testing.T) *apiStubs {
                return &apiStubs{
                    app: &stubApp{
                        methodFunc: func(ctx context.Context, gotIAM string) (SomeOutput, error) {
                            be.Equal(t, gotIAM, iamID)
                            return SomeOutput{}, errs.Newf(errs.Internal, "app error")
                        },
                    },
                }
            },
            wantStatusCode: http.StatusInternalServerError,
            wantRespBody:   `{"error":"internal","error_description":"Something went wrong"}`,
        },
    }

    for _, tc := range testCases {
        t.Run(tc.name, func(t *testing.T) {
            t.Parallel()

            req := httptest.NewRequest(tc.method, tc.path, strings.NewReader(tc.reqBody))
            if tc.prepareRequest != nil {
                req = tc.prepareRequest(req)
            }

            stubs := &apiStubs{}
            if tc.stubFactory != nil {
                stubs = tc.stubFactory(t)
            }

            recorder := httptest.NewRecorder()
            newAPIWithStubs(stubs).handlerName().ServeHTTP(recorder, req)

            assertResponse(t, recorder, tc.wantStatusCode, tc.wantRespBody)
        })
    }
}
```

## test coverage requirements

- **business logic file at least 80% coverage**
- **exclude mock\_\*.go files** (auto generated mock files)

```bash
# check coverage (exclude mock files)
go test -cover ./... -coverprofile=coverage.out
go tool cover -func=coverage.out | grep -v mock_

# generate HTML report
go tool cover -html=coverage.out
```

